  "description": "TOLXID crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C57 H58 Er4 N16 O12 4+,3(C1 H4 O1),4(N1 O3 1-),3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 4 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.730-3.791 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 107.22-112.67°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C60H67Er4N20O30. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
